From db6be419aef4cde6f39c700c17c8e53e186e192d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: arealjim <6187715+arealjim@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 12:16:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 53/54] runtime: locate hand joints in the caller's base space

xrLocateHandJointsEXT ignored XrHandJointsLocateInfoEXT::baseSpace and
returned joint poses in the runtime's world space. A caller that asks for
the joints relative to a controller's grip space (OpenComposite does, to
build the OpenVR skeleton) then received world coordinates as a
grip-relative offset, and the skeletal hand was drawn meters away from
the controller.

Locate the base space in world and express every joint in it. An unknown
or foreign base space is XR_ERROR_HANDLE_INVALID; a base space that cannot
be located reports the hand inactive.
